  "preamble": "Devoicing with aspiration turns the voiced postalveolar affricate [d͡ʒ] into the aspirated voiceless [t͡ʃʰ]. It is part of the Western Armenian consonant shift: the Classical Armenian voiced series (բ դ գ ձ ջ) became aspirated and merged with the old aspirates, so ջ /d͡ʒ/ fell together with չ /t͡ʃʰ/ (ջուր 'water' Western [t͡ʃʰuɾ]), while Eastern Armenian keeps [d͡ʒ].",
